---
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy · Quiesco"
  description="The Quiesco app collects no personal data. Readings stay on your phone and your unit."
>
  <Nav />
  <article>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 7 October 2026</p>

    <p class="lede">
      The Quiesco app does not collect, send or share any personal data on its own. There is no account, no server and no
      analytics. What the sensor measures stays on your phone and on your Quiesco unit.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app stores, and where</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Readings</strong>: carbon dioxide, temperature, humidity, light and noise levels downloaded from
        your unit. They are kept in a database on your phone.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your unit</strong>: its name, serial number and Bluetooth identifier, so the app can reconnect to
        it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A pairing key</strong>: a random key your unit issues when you enter its six-digit code. It is
        kept in the phone's secure storage (the iOS Keychain or the Android Keystore) and never leaves the
        device.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Settings</strong>: your temperature unit, theme and sleep window.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      None of this is sent anywhere. The noise sensor reports sound levels only; it does not record audio, and
      the app never uses your phone's microphone, camera, location or contacts.
    </p>

    <h2>Diagnostic reports</h2>
    <p>
      If something goes wrong, Settings → Send a diagnostic report shows a report you can email to us or share.
      It contains the app and phone versions, your unit's serial number, firmware and status, and the app's recent
      Bluetooth log. It never contains your readings or keys. The app shows you the whole report first, and it is
      only sent if you send it from your own mail app. We use it only to answer you, and delete it on request.
    </p>

    <h2>Bluetooth</h2>
    <p>
      The app uses Bluetooth only to find, pair with and read your Quiesco unit. On Android it asks for
      Bluetooth permission and declares that it does not use Bluetooth to work out your location.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      The app contains no advertising, tracking or analytics code and no crash reporting. Apple and Google may
      collect data about app downloads and crashes under their own privacy policies, according to your device
      settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Keeping or deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      Your readings stay until you remove them. Forgetting a unit in the app's Settings tab deletes its readings
      and pairing key from your phone, and uninstalling the app deletes everything. A factory reset in the app
      also erases the log stored on the unit.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The app collects no personal information from anyone, including children.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page with a new date. The app's source
      code is public on <a href={LINKS.github}>GitHub</a>, so you can check what it does.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy or the app: <a href={LINKS.support}>info@impossiblelabs.xyz</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  article {
    max-width: 42em;
    padding-block: 40px 96px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 52px);
    font-weight: 300;
  }
  .updated {
    margin-top: 8px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .lede {
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-size: 18px;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 40px;
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  p,
  ul {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }
  li + li {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
</style>
